2. DESIGNATION
Extract the formal role/title of the signoff person. 
CRITICAL OVERRIDE RULE: You MUST first read the preamble and introductory paragraphs (e.g., clauses starting with "THE UNDERSIGNED"). If the document collectively defines the capacity of the signers in the opening text (e.g., stating they are the "managing directors of the Company and together constituting the entire board"), you MUST extract this collective definition (e.g., "Managing Director of the Board") as the Designation.
NEGATIVE CONSTRAINT: Do NOT extract generic titles found immediately below the signature lines (such as "Director - Legal Representative", "Authorized Signatory", etc.) if a more descriptive collective title exists in the document's preamble. 
Only fallback to the text immediately next to/below the signature line if the preamble completely fails to define their capacity. If it cannot be determined anywhere, set "NA".
